READINGS, both direct from the table above:
  1. The series CVC exists to minimise moves in the SAME direction, with the same shape and
     the same magnitude, in the run that has NO CVC. Every window agrees inside 1 HAC SE;
     the 21-120 slopes are +0.000033 (a4) against +0.000023 (incumbent), and a4's LEVEL is
     0.002313 nats HIGHER. There is no measurable CVC descent on the CVC objective.
  2. Over steps 21-120 the gap's movement is carried almost entirely by the ROLLOUT term
     (-0.80 nats in both runs), not by the training term (-0.035 a4, -0.018 incumbent).
     CE-mode CVC is attached to the static term of the gap, and the moving term is the one
     it does not touch.

